.TH CLEVOD 8 "2026-10-11" "clevo-cc-linux 0.2.2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
clevod \- privileged Clevo fan, keyboard and battery control daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clevod
[\fB\-\-driver\fR]
[\fB\-\-mock\fR \fIFIxture\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPath\fR]
[\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR \fIMs\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-poll\fR]
[\fB\-\-session\-bus\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clevod
controls the Clevo DCHU fan controller, keyboard lighting and battery charging
interfaces. It polls the embedded controller, caches the last reading with an explicit
freshness state
.RI ( fresh / stale / unknown ),
persists user choices in a versioned TOML file, and serves
.B org.clevo.CC
on the system D\-Bus. The graphical UI and the CLI's dbus transport are clients;
the CLI also offers direct driver and read-only acpi-call transports.
.PP
Reads are open to any local user. The write methods
.BR SetFanMode (),
.BR SetPerfMode ()
are authorized through PolicyKit (actions
.BR org.clevo.CC.set\-fan\-mode
and
.BR org.clevo.CC.set\-perf\-mode );
when no authority is available they fall back to root only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-driver
Use the
.B clevo-cc
kernel driver sysfs/hwmon backend (read and write). This is the enabled write
path. Without it the daemon uses the read-only
.B acpi_call
backend for fan control. Standard power-supply interfaces remain available
independently of the fan transport.
.TP
.BI \-\-mock " Fixture"
Replay a recorded fixture instead of touching hardware; never writes.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " Path"
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/clevo\-cc/clevod.toml ).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval\-ms " Ms"
Poll interval in milliseconds (default 2000).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-poll
Do not start the background poll loop.
.TP
.B \-\-session\-bus
Bind to the per-user session bus instead of the system bus (testing).
.SH D\-BUS INTERFACE
Service
.BR org.clevo.CC ,
object
.BR /org/clevo/CC ,
interface
.BR org.clevo.CC .
.PP
Curve methods:
.B GetCurve
returns the current curve as JSON,
.B SetCurve
writes one (command 14) and selects
.BR custom .
The
.B FactoryCurve
property returns the curve the machine shipped with, or an empty string when it
has not been captured. It is captured from the EC on a cold boot, before any
write, because the firmware cannot restore it afterwards; a warm restart (where
the EC still holds the daemon's own curve) is deliberately not captured.
.PP
Power methods:
.B GetPower
reads battery, standard or native charge-window and platform-profile information
as JSON independently of fan polling. Missing readings remain unknown.
.B SetChargeThresholds
takes a battery name, start and end percentages; start=255 preserves an
existing start threshold. It requires
.B org.clevo.CC.set\-charge\-thresholds
authorization, checks readback and attempts restoration on failure.
Unsupported devices return NotSupported and invalid windows return InvalidArgs.
.PP
.B SetChargeWindow
takes the battery name, start byte, end byte and enabled boolean, using the same
PolicyKit action as SetChargeThresholds. Native FlexiCharger is bound to the
matching ACPI battery path and validates firmware-advertised discrete percentages.
Disabling retains the window. Standard threshold interfaces reject the native
enabled option. Successful readback confirms the saved firmware variables;
actual charging stop/restart behavior requires a complete charge-cycle test.
.PP
Desktop profile transitions are observed by the background poll and persisted;
using
.B \-\-no\-poll
disables this automatic synchronization. UI/CLI only change the clevo-cc provider;
desktop integration also depends on an available desktop power service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/clevo-cc/clevod.toml
Versioned daemon configuration (schema v7). Fan mode, performance mode, keyboard
settings and the custom fan curve are saved after successful writes. When
.B apply_on_start
is true, saved settings are re-applied on startup; the curve is written before the
.BR custom
mode is selected.
Successful charge thresholds are stored per battery in charge_thresholds,
including the optional native enabled state, and restored when apply_on_start
is true. Failed writes do not replace the saved threshold configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clevo-cc (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR busctl (1)
